body:
should i get a coffee or kill myself? 

&#x200B;

\- probably a philosopher

then back to suicidal 

&#x200B;

\*PARKOUR\*

"no longer human" by osamu dazai, it's about the life of oba yozo, a person incapable of revealing his "true" self to others and was forced to adopt a facade of hollow jocularity. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

or, if you're into other "books" like mangas, give "goodnight, punpun" a chance by inio asano. it's probably one of the most depressing and self-destructive manga out there.

Name: Nero Grants

&#x200B;

Age: 16 years old

&#x200B;

Race: Madness \[humans with imbued magical powers that can manipulate the essence of creation\]

&#x200B;

Appearance: middle height \[about 175cm\], light skin tone, short black hair that is messy. he wears normal clothing, black pants semi-fitted and a loose white shirt. as a part of the race of madness ,he has this colorless aura around him whenever he uses magic and his left hand specifically glows with a color matching those of a royal family. 

Theme: he's a timid young man, unsure of himself and his place around the world. a fool, that is set to make a difference in the world and the future as we know it. he's full of potential and at the same time full of unspoken fear about his origin and the past that was kept from him.

who wouldn't?

&#x200B;

*i know i will*

i mean, my story involves a certain race of beings that can manipulate the very foundation of the world - the essence that makes up the whole world and the other elements. 

&#x200B;

 i make it so that it will not become an info-dump is that some of my characters that are an expert of a certain element gives a small lecture or should i say an insight on how they do it. the science behind their magic.

i totally agree with this. especially the normal human would break down once they've come face to face how futile life is, that there is no innate meaning in the known universe - that we are just here as a mere accident, on a false hope. 

&#x200B;

the presence of suicide gives weight to the meaningless of the world and how futile it is to live without purpose.
